 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation, and its repeats of words and lines. Where the print differs from the libretto the words follow the print: \"Io sento mi gelar\" (two words; libretto sentomi), \"questo acciar\" (libretto quest'acciar), \"o ciel\" and \"o Dei\" (libretto Oh / oh: IPA ˈɔ, the interjection), \"che sei un buffone\" (libretto se'), \"Bizarra è in ver\" (libretto Bizzarra è inver; IPA bidˈdzar.ra, the word as spoken), \"Colla marmorea testa\" (some librettos Con la), \"quà\" for qua/qui. Words sung on more notes than syllables follow the notes (\"non i-o\", bar 40: ˈi.o). The Commendatore sings only \"Sì!\" (bar 84). IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S54) and the IPA was checked against Castel. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
